  "setting": "聽得見水聲的河岸",
  "subtitle": "",
  "subtitle_en": "",
  "lead": "她帶著空白的貝葉走進河岸，學習一根弦，也學習人群、器物與水的聲音。",
  "lead_en": "She enters the river country with blank palm leaves, learning one string, then the sounds of people, objects and water.",
  "statement": "她帶著空白的貝葉走進河岸，學習一根弦，也學習人群、器物與水的聲音。\n\n辯才天女與知識、音樂、河流相連的意象，在這本書裡成為一段反覆傾聽的旅程。她把貝葉上的線、器物的顫動與水面的紋路連起來，讓尚未命名的聲音抵達他人。\n\n有些聲音先抵達別人，才回到發聲的人身上。最後一張停在下一個音將要出現的時候。",
  "statement_en": "She enters the river country with blank palm leaves, learning one string, then the sounds of people, objects and water.\n\nIn this book, the imagery of Saraswati, linked with knowledge, music and rivers, becomes a journey of listening again and again. She connects the lines on palm leaves, the vibrations of objects and the patterns on water, letting sounds that have yet to be named reach others.\n\nSome sounds reach others before returning to the person who made them. The final image pauses as another note is about to arrive.",
  "afterword": "有些聲音先抵達別人，才回到發聲的人身上。最後一張停在下一個音將要出現的時候。",
  "afterword_en": "Some sounds reach others before returning to the person who made them. The final image pauses as another note is about to arrive.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "",
  "story_en": "",
